From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: add g16_replay to write template
 values into compute records

To find which bytes of a compute command make another driver's commands
run differently from ours, it helps to submit our commands with that
driver's values in selected fields and change one group of fields at a
time.

Add a write-only template, the aurora-g16/replay debugfs file, which takes
a small blob of (record, piece, offset, width, value, step) entries for the
compute sequence record, and a runtime mask, g16_replay. While a piece's
bit is set, every compute command's sequence record takes the template
value for that piece's fields, or value + step * n for counter fields,
after this driver has filled it; the embedded copy in the work object
gets the same bytes. Clearing one bit removes one piece without a reload.

Fields this driver fills with an address are refused when the blob is
written, so addresses always stay this driver's, and a malformed blob is
refused and leaves nothing armed. The stats file gains a replay line with
the mask, the entries, the commands written and the blobs refused.

The default of 0 writes nothing.

Assisted-by: LLM
